# Dev-mode env (COMMITTED — shared convention). Loaded ONLY by `electron-vite dev`
# (Vite mode=development). A production build does NOT load this file.
#
# ⚠️ There is NO local value here, on purpose (product decision, 01/09/2026): a developer's
# `pnpm dev` runs against the SAME public services as an installed app — the common
# Supabase (sign-in), the common analytics relay, the common releases feed and the common
# Sentry — filled by default in `scripts/publicServices.ts` and stamped
# env:"development" / packaged:false so the boards can filter them. Everything that is
# BILLING-gated (backend, admin console, gateway) stays absent, exactly as in a build from
# the sources: no accounts API, no organizations, no server-side redaction.
#
# ── Pointing dev at your OWN services is an explicit choice ───────────────────────────
# Put the overrides in `apps/desktop/.env.development.local` (gitignored, highest Vite
# precedence — a VITE_* variable always wins over the baked table, `appEnv.ts`). The
# usual reason is to mute a public default or aim sign-in at your own project:
#
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-ref>.supabase.co   # your own project, not the brand's
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your publishable key>
#   VITE_ANALYTICS_RELAY_URL=                          # empty = no analytics from this machine
#   OPENMASQ_SENTRY_DSN=                               # empty = no crash reports from this machine
#
# ⚠️ The backend, admin console and gateway are NOT in this repository — they live in the
# private `infra` repo — so there is no local stack to bring up here, and `OPENMASQ_BILLING`
# stays off (no accounts API, organizations or server-side redaction) whatever you set. The
# renderer CSP (dev-only Vite plugin) allows http://localhost:* if you run your own.
#
# Versions tab: releases come from the feed above, on the channel `VITE_UPDATES_CHANNEL`
# (read from the SHELL env at dev launch, not from this file). Default channel
# `desktop-stable`; to browse the candidate history: VITE_UPDATES_CHANNEL=desktop-beta pnpm dev.
# Real update checks are packaged-only (`src/main/updates/index.ts`): dev never updates itself.
#
# ── YOUR OWN infrastructure ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supply these at BUILD time (CI or shell) to switch each capability ON, or set one EMPTY
# to opt out of a public default. Full runbook: SELF_HOSTING.md.
#   OPENMASQ_SUPABASE_URL=              # https://<ref>.supabase.co — accounts / auth
#   OPENMASQ_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=  # sb_publishable_…
#   OPENMASQ_BILLING=1                  # THE gate: without it the four addresses below are
#                                       # baked EMPTY even if supplied, and nothing is sold
#                                       # (scripts/buildDefines.ts). Auth, Slack relay,
#                                       # analytics, releases and Sentry are NOT behind it.
#   OPENMASQ_BACKEND_URL=               # the API (billing, sync, organizations, feedback)
#   OPENMASQ_BACKEND_URL_STAGING=       # same, for a second environment (optional)
#   OPENMASQ_GATEWAY_URL=               # server-side redaction + platform-served models
#   OPENMASQ_GATEWAY_URL_STAGING=       # same, for a second environment (optional)
#   OPENMASQ_AUTH_URL=                  # the apps/auth relay (Slack connector only)
#   VITE_UPDATES_URL=                   # the apps/updates feed
#   OPENMASQ_SENTRY_DSN=                # crash reports
#   OPENMASQ_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=          # GitHub connector — publisher's app by default
#                                       #   (publicServices.ts); set your own, or empty
#                                       #   (`X=`) for « non configuré »
#   OPENMASQ_SLACK_CLIENT_ID=           # Slack connector — same default, with OPENMASQ_AUTH_URL
#   OPENMASQ_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=          # Google connector ("Desktop app" client, PKCE)
#   OPENMASQ_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=      # same — non-confidential for a Desktop client
#   OPENMASQ_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=       # Microsoft connector — same default (multi-tenant)
#   OPENMASQ_POSTHOG_KEY=               # analytics web (@openmasq/analytics, sites)
